# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides for the machine-wide gitignore.
#
# The global file at %USERPROFILE%\.gitignore is a Unity one, where .csproj and
# .sln really are generated artifacts and are correctly excluded. For a normal
# .NET repository that rule is fatal: without project files nobody who clones
# this can build it. Repository rules are evaluated after global ones, so these
# put the files back.
#
# The global file is left alone on purpose. It is right for what it was written
# for.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
!*.csproj
!*.sln
!*.slnx
!*.props
!*.targets

# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
publish/

# What the release ritual writes locally. dist/ is where packaging/build-dist.ps1 puts the two
# archives, their bills of materials and the sums - about 270 MB of it - and build/signing is
# where packaging/sign-release.ps1 unpacks and signs. Neither is source, and the archives a user
# downloads are made by the workflow on a tag rather than here.
#
# NOTE FOR ANYONE READING THE RULE BELOW THIS BLOCK: `packages/` is a NuGet rule and does NOT
# cover `packaging/`, which is source and is committed. Two words one letter apart, doing
# opposite things.
dist/
build/

# Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Test and coverage output
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage
*.trx

# The one coverage file that is INPUT rather than output: the floors the gate holds the
# measurement against. It has to travel with the repository, because CI reads it and CI cannot
# see tools/. Without this line the rule above hides it, which is how it was found - the file was
# written, committed nothing, and would have left the workflow with no floor to read.
!tests/coverage-floor.json

# NuGet
*.nupkg
packages/

# Local tooling and scratch
.claude/
_scratch/
*.local.json

# Working documentation. Deliberately outside version control: the owner keeps and
# versions it separately. Consequences are spelled out in CLAUDE.md itself, section
# "Dokumenty" - the short version is that git will never show you that a document
# changed, so document changes have to be reported by hand.
#
# CLAUDE.md is excluded for the same reason. It still works: it is read from disk,
# not from git.
#
# A public repository will eventually need its own README, written for contributors
# and independent of these files.
docs/
CLAUDE.md

# Developer tools.  Anything here that matters has to be described in docs/ well enough to be rebuilt from the description.
tools/

# The developer changelog. 
CHANGELOG-DEV.md

# Python bytecode. Nothing here runs Python as part of the product - the two files that
# exist are gates CI runs from a checkout - but importing one of them locally to test it
# writes a cache directory beside it, and on 2026-09-22 one of those .pyc files was
# committed without anybody noticing. Machine-specific bytes in a public repository, from
# a language this project does not ship.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
